{"title":"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_22\">Problem 22</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 22\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given an equilateral triangle with side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, consider the locus of all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd35d2132efec91a307601a61b698575db4ce8cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathit{P}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> in the plane of the \ntriangle such that the sum of the squares of the distances from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd35d2132efec91a307601a61b698575db4ce8cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathit{P}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> to the vertices of the triangle is a fixed number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. This locus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50c70f5a8c44ad350b4f4cae140d509f1fc1e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\text{is a circle if }a&gt;s^2\\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(B) }\\text{contains only three points if }a=2s^2\\text{ and is a circle if }a&gt;2s^2\\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(C) }\\text{is a circle with positive radius only if }s^2&lt;a&lt;2s^2\\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(D) }\\text{contains only a finite number of points for any value of }a\\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(E) }\\text{is none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"487\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we define point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bdaeefab4bbcbf87ab70956c5caa62d5aab8c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathit{P} = (x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />, and the three points of the triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31eb8f62b96b6091adc66eb90d68832a3b446be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = (x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d82918e85864529f4ce9b512c3d1588b505925.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 = (x_2,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a28730863cdf433c535cbb1b103722903d46d10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3 = (x_3,y_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, then we have two equations to work with.  \n</p><p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd35d2132efec91a307601a61b698575db4ce8cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathit{P}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> must satisfy the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55de8850035f953ed7d68688dedf17d2be5d19eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P - P_1|^2 + |P - P_2|^2 + |P - P_3|^2 =\\newline [(x-x_1)^2+(y-y_1)^2]+[(x-x_2)^2+(y-y_2)^2]+[(x-x_3)^2+(y-y_3)^2] = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Second, the fact that the three sides of the triangle all have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> gives us:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/62366e41142ae5400fe498cecd160ddd3c872318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P_2 - P_1|^2 + |P_3 - P_2|^2 + |P_1 - P_3|^2 =\\newline [(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2]+[(x_3-x_2)^2+(y_3-y_2)^2]+[(x_1-x_3)^2+(y_1-y_3)^2] = 3s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Define the center of the triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70d6b5da612f74f5d9dd7d84c216f00ddf1a13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_C = (x_C, y_C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />.  \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad3073392f5d46e63c5625d5ab337e0f0bb1279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_C = \\frac{x_1+x_2+x_3}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696c03b39bb4d5c786e052736ddcb441a024dc2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_C = \\frac{y_1+y_2+y_3}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />.  \n</p><p>Also note that the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e17d85b5f5e7a48245e2662246a88ed0d253b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> and each of the triangle vertices is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3ae1d6ecc701685e7c4bb7d3d6d03d0d76c6ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"43\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/2250f61bee7702221b42f4530220bb1b136a31af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P_C - P_1|^2 + |P_C - P_2|^2 + |P_C - P_3|^2 =\\newline [(x_C-x_1)^2+(y_C-y_1)^2]+[(x_C-x_2)^2+(y_C-y_2)^2]+[(x_C-x_3)^2+(y_C-y_3)^2] = s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493e6eda8787f737324121b5cbbe3b76d0c7cc5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-x_1) = (x - x_C) + (x_C - x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"257\" height=\"20\" />, and similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73ad2be5083a149848171accd00634cf04b68935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y-y_1), (x-x_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />, etc.\n</p><p>Now expanding the first sum and using the second sum, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/44708252a7acc8ba27bc820db2f10d8f00635064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3[(x-x_C)^2+(y-y_C)^2] + s^2\\newline  + 2(x - x_C)[(x_C - x_1) + (x_C - x_2) + (x_C - x_3)] + 2(y - y_C)[(y_C - y_1) + (y_C - y_2) + (y_C - y_3)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e17d85b5f5e7a48245e2662246a88ed0d253b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is centroid of the triangle, its coordinates are the averages of the coordinates of the three points.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f65921ae059cb6e7a9e3da7ed70c37fb8aef8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x_C = x_1 + x_2 + x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"17\" />, and the latter parts of the above equations are zero.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a698fc4c8e49f60f3f8f832f6d2a7e18284274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - s^2 = 3[(x-x_C)^2+(y-y_C)^2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This means that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56ee8df62e4e124248a1cd5ac5e614554903bdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, the locus of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will be a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e17d85b5f5e7a48245e2662246a88ed0d253b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>This problem could be also solved with coordinate geometry, where we place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> at the origin and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> along the positive x-axis, or even let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e17d85b5f5e7a48245e2662246a88ed0d253b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the origin and place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> along the negative x-axis.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME\" title=\"1976 AHSME\">1976 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1976 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1976\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172139\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 233/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6799/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.408      1 -total\n 57.87%    7.181      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.74%    4.931      1 Template:M